// a single `available`, and F2/F3 had simply not been given one — so they read
// 0/9 on every engine while both were computing correctly. A single flag also
// cannot tell the two questions apart that the verdict has to answer:
//
//   inputPresent — the STRUCTURE this fact needs exists in this session. Its
//                  absence across every session of an engine is what
//                  `UNAVAILABLE:<engine>` means.
//   fired        — the fact produced at least one row here. A fact can be
//                  perfectly derivable and legitimately fire zero times,
//                  because the session contained no loop and no churn. Zero
//                  firings is not evidence of a missing field.
const anyWrite = allTools.some((t) => (t.toolClass === 'edit' || t.toolClass === 'write') && t.filePath !== undefined);
